This class uses the `OrderedDict` from the `collections` module to maintain the order of keys. The `__init__` method initializes the cache with a specified capacity. 

The `get` method retrieves a value associated with a given key. If the key does not exist, it returns -1. Otherwise, it moves the accessed key to the end of the list using `move_to_end()` method and returns the value.

The `put` method inserts a new key-value pair into the cache. If the key already exists, it updates its value and moves it to the end of the list. If the cache is full (i.e., its size exceeds the capacity), it removes the least recently used item using `popitem(last=False)` method and inserts the new key-value pair.

This implementation ensures that the most recently accessed items are always at the end of the dictionary, while the least recently accessed items are moved to the beginning when the cache reaches its capacity.
